# ref-a2e4816-speculative-sphere-sphere
# A slow sphere closes on a static sphere from just outside contact, with no
# gravity. The step is too short to make the sphere fast, so the pair is
# eligible for contact recycling. A sphere-sphere routine without a speculative
# margin left the pair empty and recycling then let the sphere sink without a
# contact (discussion #175). The speculative margin (box3d a2e4816) reports the
# pair inside the speculative distance, so the sphere stops at the surface.
# Reference: vanilla float box3d at upstream commit a2e4816.
# Observable: the approaching sphere's final height (it must not sink past the
#   surface) and the contact count.
expect pos 0.002 rot 0.001 vel 0.01 horizon 20 counts exact
world gravity 0 0 0 dt 1 60 substeps 4 steps 20
body static position 0 0 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
shape 0 sphere 0.5 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
body dynamic position 0 0.755 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 -0.6 0 angvel 0 0 0
shape 1 sphere 0.25 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
